-oncogene that is associated with MEN2A and influences the clinical management of patients with this condition.", "NIVELES DE RIESGO:Niveles de riesgo refers to the classification of RET mutations into different risk categories for developing medullary thyroid carcinoma and other associated conditions.", "CRIBADO BIOQUÍMICO:Cribado bioquímico refers to biochemical screening for conditions such as pheochromocytoma and hyperparathyroidism in patients with MEN syndromes.", "M918T:", "RET PROTO-ONCOGENE:The RET proto-oncogene is crucial for the development of MEN2 syndromes, with different mutations associated with varying risks of tumor development.", "WELLS ET AL.:Wells and colleagues revised the American Thyroid Association guidelines for the management of medullary thyroid carcinoma, contributing to the understanding of thyroid cancer management.", "VALDÉS GALLEGO:", "HYPERPARATHYROIDISM PRIMARIO:Primary hyperparathyroidism is a condition often associated with MEN1 and MEN2 syndromes, characterized by excessive secretion of parathyroid hormone.", "MICROADENOMA HIPOFISARIO:Microadenoma hipofisario is a small tumor located on the pituitary gland. It is noteworthy that the patient's mother had a microadenoma hipofisario, which was successfully resolved with treatment. This type of tumor can produce hormones, including prolactin, and is frequently examined in relation to multiple endocrine neoplasia (MEN) syndromes.", "SINDROME MEN1:MEN1 syndrome is characterized by the triad of primary hyperparathyroidism, pituitary tumors, and pancreatic endocrine tumors."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}